MiniMax-M3.1-Flash on four DGX Sparks (TP4)

Repository-authored launch scripts, tests and documentation: MIT, see LICENSE.

Apache-2.0 portions (full licence text in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt), each marked in its file header:
- roce/mm31_roce/: adapted from vLLM (vllm-project/vllm, Apache-2.0) distributed-communication hooks
  and from the RoCEnante one-shot RDMA all-reduce by Local Inference Lab (Luke Alonso, Jason Cook),
  as shipped in FlashInfer's b12x package (Apache-2.0); first adapted for GLM-5.3 TP4 in our
  GLM recipe. The RoCEnante code itself is not vendored here; it is used from the FlashInfer build
  inside the serving image.
- overlay/: b12x paged sparse-attention binding for vLLM's MiniMax-M3 path (uses FlashInfer's
  experimental b12x, Apache-2.0); overlay/gb10check/mm31_triton_kernels.py contains Triton kernels
  extracted from vLLM (Apache-2.0) for static compile checks.
- sglang/: import-time patches to SGLang (sgl-project/sglang, Apache-2.0) source and the RoCEnante
  hook for SGLang's TP group (shares roce/mm31_roce).

No model weights or container images are distributed. The MiniMax-M3.1-Flash weights are under the
MiniMax Community License.
